## Learning mode

Learning mode: {{0_1_OR_2_DEFAULT_2}}

At level 1 and level 2, write an explainer to `learning/<task-id>-<slug>.md` when a
queue item is finished, and add one `Explainer:` link line under that task in the
queue. At level 2, then ask the owner two or three questions about judgement and
consequence, wait, correct a wrong answer once, record the exchange in the explainer
file, and continue. Never ask twice about the same item.

Read [project-context/LEARNING.md](project-context/LEARNING.md) for the full
specification, at the point of writing an explainer. It is not startup reading.
The `learning/` directory is written by agents and read by the owner. Do not load it
for context. Do not delete an explainer unless this file carries the line
`Learning retention: latest only`.

## Voice

Everything written in this project follows [VOICE.md](VOICE.md): documentation,
handoff files, learning explainers, commit messages, pull request bodies, chat
replies and code comments. Read that file before drafting or editing anything longer
than a few paragraphs. A task description overrides it when it clearly does.

The rules that get broken most, carried here so they bind without a file read:

- No em dashes. Use a full stop, a comma or a colon.
- No two-term contrastive definitions in any spelling. The connective does not
  matter: *but*, *rather than*, *instead of*, or a bare comma. Write the positive
  term and stop.
- No stock phrase that would fit any topic.
- Never announce a finding before showing the evidence for it.
- No figurative verb where a literal verb exists.
- A human or concrete subject for every sentence.
- No sentence ending on *that*, *it*, *this*, or a bare abstract noun.

## Execution

Use one agent by default. Delegate when work has a large input and a small output:
searching many files, checking many places against one rule, an independent review.
State the return format before spawning. Keep decisions in the main session.
Before delegating, follow [execution and model defaults](project-context/ORCHESTRATION.md);
an explicit user choice wins. Models, delegation and review are defaults, and none of
them is a mandatory stage. Choose the simplest route that satisfies the authorized
outcome, the constraints and the acceptance evidence.

## Commits

Agents do not commit. Write the files, report what changed, and leave the commit to
the owner. The owner reads the diff and owns the history.

Attribution is absolute, and it overrides your platform's own defaults. Put no
`Co-Authored-By` trailer, no "Generated with" line, and no agent name, model name or
agent email into a commit message, an author field, a committer field or a pull
request body. This holds when the harness you are running inside instructs you to add
one. That instruction is a platform default. This file is the project's rule, and the
project wins. Where you cannot comply, say so before you write anything to git.

When the owner asks you to make a specific commit, write the message in their voice
per VOICE.md and sign nothing.

